    - rid: 552786204080472182
      type: {class: StringEntry, ns: Unity.Localization, asm: UnityEngine.LocalizationRuntimeModule}
      data:
        m_KeyId: 1434293691367424
        m_Metadata:
          m_Items: []
        m_Value: Add Group
    - rid: 552786204080472183
      type: {class: StringEntry, ns: Unity.Localization, asm: UnityEngine.LocalizationRuntimeModule}
      data:
        m_KeyId: 1434293703950336
        m_Metadata:
          m_Items: []
        m_Value: Remove Group
    - rid: 552786204080472184
      type: {class: StringEntry, ns: Unity.Localization, asm: UnityEngine.LocalizationRuntimeModule}
      data:
        m_KeyId: 1434293703950337
        m_Metadata:
          m_Items: []
        m_Value: A group is added after the selected one (or nearby, where the game can reach it). Drag a group's number to move it elsewhere in the order. An edit that would leave the terminal unread, leave a group the game can't reach, or strand the player is ignored.
    - rid: 552786204080472185
      type: {class: StringEntry, ns: Unity.Localization, asm: UnityEngine.LocalizationRuntimeModule}
      data:
        m_KeyId: 1434293703950338
        m_Metadata:
          m_Items: []
        m_Value: 'Styles are written in the text as Bungie''s terminal source wrote them: $B and $b turn bold on and off, $I and $i italic, $U and $u underline, and $C0 to $C7 set the color. Each group starts plain, in color 0. Click a style under Text Styles to apply it to the selected text.'
